WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.407
- Say hello to John Hamm!

00:00:02.407 --> 00:00:03.720
(audience cheers)

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.387
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.368
- [John] Hey!

00:00:24.368 --> 00:00:25.407
- You look fabulous.

00:00:25.407 --> 00:00:27.450
I'm just gonna lead with that.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.590
- Fired up.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.910
- Wait, you have like a...

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.980
You should have a like glasses deal.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.021
- Ah, I don't know, maybe-

00:00:33.021 --> 00:00:33.854
- [Kelly] I'm just saying.

00:00:33.854 --> 00:00:35.040
- Maybe my deal is just wearing glasses.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.300
- I'm just saying why
you should look in it,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.720
it could be a lucrative
business, it's a nice look.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.220
So Elisabeth Moss, as you saw

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.100
we know she beat you
like every time, right?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.510
- I don't know about every time.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.860
I think what she said was she beat me once

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.510
and then I refused to play again.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.610
But yeah, it was the championship.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.980
She won the championship and
then the championship was over.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.740
And then, you know, there was
never another championship.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.850
What a shame.
(audience laughing)

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.530
- That is so sad.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.540
No, what was the game of choice again?

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.070
- Well, she played speed,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.840
but we played a lot of games at the Mad...

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.300
In the Mad Man base camp,
there was dominoes,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.757
there was a lot of cards,
there was heads up.

00:01:10.757 --> 00:01:12.451
- Do you do Mexican train dominoes?

00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:13.284
I love those.

00:01:13.284 --> 00:01:14.117
- We have played, we
didn't play that there

00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.480
but we did played regular old dominoes.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.700
It was, there were a lot of games

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.780
'cause there was a lot of...

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.613
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:20.446
- We spent a lot of time there.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.117
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Yeah, I worked...

00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:26.160
I was always there 'cause
I'm in every scene.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:26.993
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:26.993 --> 00:01:30.360
- So I would sort of
run the game quotient.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.970
And then if there was one that
I wasn't particularly good at

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.469
we shuffled that one into the back of the-

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:36.504
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:36.504 --> 00:01:37.337
In the back of the line.

00:01:37.337 --> 00:01:38.312
- We see who you are.
- Yes.

00:01:38.312 --> 00:01:39.960
- So wait, did you...

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.100
You also love poker, right?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.940
Do you do poker nights?

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.530
- I play poker.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.230
- I've been in a, actually a game

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.700
of poker that's been running every week

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.090
since before I started
"Mad Man", which would've been-

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.830
- [Kelly] What?
- back in the early 2000s.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.090
But no it's yeah.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.140
I love playing poker, it's fun.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.110
It's more fun to just
get your friends together

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.430
and sit around a table and talk.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.263
- [Kelly] 100%.
- Yeah.

00:02:00.263 --> 00:02:01.200
- And it's just kind of the vessel

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.235
for that whole mingling scenario.

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:03.187
- Absolutely
- Oh, okay, I love it.

00:02:03.187 --> 00:02:05.700
Wait, did you always know that
you wanted to be an actor?

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.533
Like from early on?

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:08.370
I know a lot of people kind of say that.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.203
- Kind of.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.200
I was chosen at a very early age.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.130
- [Kelly] Oh.
- In first grade

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.153
by my first grade
teacher, Shirley Kassouy.

00:02:17.153 --> 00:02:18.480
- I love that you still know her name.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.577
- If anybody wants to
double check my facts.

00:02:21.577 --> 00:02:22.410
(audience laughing)

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.490
To play Winnie the Pooh,

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:28.490
in our first grade production
of Winnie the Pooh.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.170
So, and I think Miss Kassouy picked me

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:36.170
because I had no fear
of speaking very loudly

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.550
in front of people.
- Yeah.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.901
- So yeah. I wouldn't say-

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:40.734
- [Kelly] Which isn't
normal for most kids.

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.140
- It set me down the path, you know

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.140
of dressing up in animated
costumes, but no, I think it's...

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:52.410
I've never had a problem with
standing up and talking loud.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.520
- Do you, Okay.
- And looking like an idiot.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.810
- To go even deeper.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.970
- With a pillow strapped to my stomach.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.202
- Did you get a pot of honey?

00:02:58.202 --> 00:02:59.035
(audience laughing)
- I sure did.

00:02:59.035 --> 00:03:00.088
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:00.088 --> 00:03:03.450
- No, to go even deeper, do you feel...

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.920
Feel free to not answer this,

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.100
but I feel like sometimes I'm
more comfortable on stage.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:08.933
- [John] For sure.

00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:09.766
- Yeah.
- It's fun.

00:03:09.766 --> 00:03:10.890
- I feel like I'm more comfortable.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.320
Like, I don't know if that's like trauma

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.640
in there somewhere, I
don't know what that is.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.570
- A hundred percent, by the way.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.720
- Yeah.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.360
- No, it can be fun.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.370
I mean, some people it's
the most terrifying thing

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.450
in the world and for some people

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.040
it's the opposite and I think
you and I probably like that.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:24.900
- Yeah, I am.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.777
Yeah, I feel very comfortable.
- [John] It's a Blast!

00:03:26.777 --> 00:03:27.990
- Almost more comfortable

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.640
than having to play myself sometimes

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.890
at a party or something
with other celebrities

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.330
which people think you're
all supposed to be friends.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.170
It's like what?

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.190
Anyway, but I love you.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.110
You wanna be friends?
- Yes, totally.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.380
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.230
- So before the break we
were talking about you acting

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.640
in school, but I hear that
you actually went back

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.230
to your high school and you taught acting.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.990
- I did, I actually went
back to my old high school

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.090
in St. Louis, Missouri,
John Buroughs School

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.266
in St Louis, Missouri.

00:03:49.266 --> 00:03:52.233
I'm sure some of you may
know somebody who went there.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.870
There's usually like one in every crowd.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:55.920
- [Kelly] Hmm.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.747
- In 2004, after I graduated college,

00:03:59.747 --> 00:04:02.730
I had a theater degree and no prospects.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.560
So I was like, well, what can I do?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.020
I know, I'll talk to my old acting teacher

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.930
and maybe he'll gimme a job,
teaching at my old high school.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.090
And I did that and it was really fun.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.040
I was 24 years old.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.810
I had no idea what I was doing.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:16.650
- Teaching is hard.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.790
- It is incredibly hard.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.460
And not only is it hard, it is a long day.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.293
- Yeah.

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.530
- And when you're used
to being a bartender

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.430
and a waiter and your day
starts at like 5:30, 6PM,

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.418
that eight o'clock wake up
is a little bit of a rough

00:04:29.418 --> 00:04:30.251
- Yeah.

00:04:30.251 --> 00:04:31.350
- Transition.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.960
So that was my introduction to that.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.030
I spent a whole year there,
they liked what I did.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.620
I had some really great students.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.238
Ellie Kemper was one of my students.

00:04:39.238 --> 00:04:40.071
- [Kelly] Oh wow!

00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:43.650
- I had a couple other
pretty phenomenal kids

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.060
in my classes.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:45.893
- Small world.

00:04:45.893 --> 00:04:47.160
- But, they said do you wanna come back?

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.030
You wanna keep doing this?

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.820
And I was like, well, I'm 24 years old.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:53.851
I'm pretty long in the tooth for an actor.

00:04:53.851 --> 00:04:54.684
(audience laughing)

00:04:54.684 --> 00:04:55.517
- [Kelly] Which is crazy.

00:04:55.517 --> 00:04:57.664
- Which is crazy, but I-
- Try being a woman. (laughs)

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.497
- Exactly.

00:04:59.697 --> 00:05:01.590
But I thought, if I don't do it now

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.640
I probably won't do it.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.920
- And so I was like, I
would love to do this

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.140
but I have to try, at least try.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:07.973
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:09.420
- So, I packed up my car,

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.760
which was a 1986 Toyota Corolla.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:12.593
- [Kelly] Nice.

00:05:12.593 --> 00:05:15.690
- And I got all the money
that I had, which was $150.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.670
And I headed west.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.200
- I Love...

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.580
Not as similar story I was never teacher,

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.830
but I just mean like, I think
you have those big dreams

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.663
and a lot of people do

00:05:23.663 --> 00:05:26.790
but it's a brave thing to
just drive across country

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:27.623
head out west.

00:05:27.623 --> 00:05:28.500
I'm from Texas, and I did the same.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.460
I was a cocktail waitress.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.650
So we all, we all were
waiters at some point.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.640
- Exactly, tip your waiters.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.290
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.090
But I love it to be so bold

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.200
and move out there for a dream.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.970
But how long, like...

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:39.990
'Cause you were persistent,

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.010
you persevered like you...

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.990
It was from that teaching class

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.390
to when you actually hit, like got a job.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.850
- From that acting class
to when I actually hit,

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:51.150
was a period of about probably five years.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.410
- Really?
- [John] Yeah.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.243
- That's a lot.

00:05:53.243 --> 00:05:54.076
- [John] Waiting tables and-

00:05:54.076 --> 00:05:55.200
- [Kelly] That's hard
- Bartending and everything.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.610
Yeah, well, I mean, but it was fun.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:00.270
I mean, it's fun to be in a
new city, making new friends,

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.170
learning the lay of the
land, learning, going to...

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.570
When I came to LA like the Beck

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.000
and the Silverlake music
scene was all happening,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.620
I lived over there and it was really fun.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.300
And you could go see
those shows for five bucks

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.070
and all my friends were comedians,

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.010
and you could go see
shows at Largo for $3.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.920
And if you waited in line, it was free.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:20.760
So there was all that.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:21.660
There was fun stuff to do.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.280
You just had to kind of lean into it, but-

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.113
- You were me though.

00:06:24.113 --> 00:06:25.380
Where is the free one?

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.550
- Yeah, where's the free show exactly?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.383
- [Kelly] That was me
- Which line is free?

00:06:27.383 --> 00:06:28.470
- [Kelly] When I cocktail down here.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.480
- So wait, speaking of
shows, you must love music.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.180
I heard that you were actually
at Prince's last concert.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.171
- Oh, I was.

00:06:34.171 --> 00:06:35.151
- [Kelly] How did? That's amazing.

00:06:35.151 --> 00:06:36.730
(audience applauding)

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.300
I never got to see him live.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.133
I never got to see him live.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:40.966
- Yeah, oh wow.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:42.510
There's yeah, that was it.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.460
It was him and a piano and a microphone.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.943
The tour was called "Prince:
Piano and a Microphone.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.700
And he-
- [Kelly] Very literal.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:54.300
- He played for about 90 to
a hundred minutes nonstop

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.820
and it was like, he would
start songs and then like

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.290
look out the crowd and be like, mhm

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.550
you guys aren't ready for that one yet.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.080
And the crowd would go like crazy.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:01.913
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:01.913 --> 00:07:03.120
- It was in Atlanta,
Georgia at the Fox theater

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.410
which is this old beautiful.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.402
- Yeah.
- You probably played there.

00:07:05.402 --> 00:07:06.235
- Yeah, I love it.

00:07:06.235 --> 00:07:09.090
- Vaudeville theater,
right in Midtown there.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.010
And it was like church.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:11.843
It was-
- [Kelly] Spiritual.

00:07:11.843 --> 00:07:13.890
- People turned up and it was really fun.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:14.723
It had been...

00:07:14.723 --> 00:07:16.740
I had gotten tickets.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.150
I was shooting "Baby Driver."

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.200
You don't have to applaud for that.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.614
But it is a good movie.

00:07:20.614 --> 00:07:22.633
( Kelly and John laugh)

00:07:22.633 --> 00:07:24.660
(audience applauds)

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:25.493
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:07:25.493 --> 00:07:27.063
- I'm only putting this in context,

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.690
but we were shooting "Baby Driver"

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:31.800
and I saw that he was coming

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.350
and I knew that he was coming
on this particular tour.

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.680
He was playing by himself

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.020
and I thought, I'm gonna, I got tickets.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.510
And he canceled.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:39.343
- Oh.

00:07:39.343 --> 00:07:40.408
- He got sick and he canceled.

00:07:40.408 --> 00:07:42.720
And I was like, oh no, but he rescheduled.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.090
And he rescheduled for
the end of our shoot

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.320
and I still had those days off.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.620
So I was like, okay, my
tickets are still good.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.030
We're gonna get to go.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.020
And it was his last show

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.970
and I still have my little ticket stub.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.350
- Oh my gosh, that's incredible.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:58.150
- And it was the best show
I've ever seen, it was great.

